From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Omer Dangoor <omerdn1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 19:34:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Remove PostHog analytics

Events went to us.i.posthog.com unless MAESTRO_CLI_NO_ANALYTICS was set
or ~/.maestro/analytics.json said no, so a fresh machine reported every
command. Login also called api.copilot.mobile.dev for the user and org
to identify them in PostHog.

The posthog-server dependency is gone and Analytics is now an object
whose methods do nothing. Upstream's trackEvent calls stay where they
are, so this patch doesn't touch the commands that make them. Cloud
requests no longer carry the analytics id as X-UUID. The first-run
"Anonymous analytics enabled" notice goes too.
